Context for 7848b5d (T036): MVP_SPEC.md section 12 states the two rules this task wires end to end: store no raw case content by default, and keep credentials out of default logs and committed artifacts. Most of the boundary already existed by construction (the report case block holds identifier and input hash only, the Jev adapter sanitizes provider errors to class, status, and request identifier, profiles reject api_key and case bodies since T028), so the work was to close the one real gap, pin the rest with canaries, and record the defaults as contract text. The gap was replay provenance: hashing.md already said replaying a run needs the host snapshots and the stored reports, but no field could name a snapshot. The additive change adds case.snapshot, one host-controlled reference of 1 to 256 characters, because a longer reference could smuggle case content and the host cannot be asked to shorten a real storage key below a useful length; the bound is enforced at the same parse boundary that reads offered attempt bindings, so the Node binding and the stored-report parser get it for free. The reference is deliberately provenance, not identity: the drift guard still compares id and input_hash, because the same input replayed from a different snapshot is the same case. The canary suite drives the public run path rather than isolated units: the canary strings sit in the case input, so a passing run proves the sensitive content was really assessed and the report still holds none of it, which unit-level assertions cannot show. The wrapper-level snapshot rejection lands at createRunState, before rule assessment, so no evaluator spend precedes it. One honest limit stayed: a host adapter that throws an error quoting its own case content still crosses verbatim, because the wrapper cannot know which host strings are private; the shipped adapters sanitize, the evaluator contract states the obligation, and the canary pins the Jev path. The vitest worker SIGBUS seen during verification is environmental (confirmed on the unmodified baseline); --maxWorkers=1 runs the full suite green.
